#!/bin/bash
# land-three-photos.sh — the skin & hair assessment asks for three photos
# instead of six, and takes them from a camera, a file, or a drag.
#
# FRONTEND ONLY (together-city-react). The server never named an angle.
set -euo pipefail

cd "$(dirname "$0")"
[ -d together-city-react ] || { echo "!! Run this from the Together-Ai repo root."; exit 1; }

if [ -f .git/index.lock ] && [ ! -s .git/index.lock ]; then
  echo "== clearing a stale empty .git/index.lock"
  rm -f .git/index.lock
fi

NEEDS="Three photographs, taken however suits you"
case "$(git log --oneline -40)" in
  *"$NEEDS"*) echo "== \"$NEEDS\" is already here. Nothing to do."; exit 0 ;;
esac

ALLOWED='^ M together-city-react/(public/assets/img/(apple-touch-icon-180|tc-icon-1024|tc-icon-192|tc-icon-512|tc-icon-maskable-512)\.png|public/downloads/TogetherCity\.apk)$'
DIRTY="$(git status --porcelain \
  | grep -Ev '^\?\? (land-.*\.sh|push-.*\.sh|.*\.patch)$' \
  | grep -Ev "$ALLOWED" || true)"
if [ -n "$DIRTY" ]; then
  echo "!! The tree carries changes this script did not expect:"; echo "$DIRTY"; exit 1
fi

PATCH="$(mktemp "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/land.XXXXXX")"
trap 'rm -f "$PATCH"' EXIT
cat <<'B64EOF' | tr -d '\n' | openssl base64 -d -A > "$PATCH"

B64EOF
WANT="b1d6664cc065433b768b9928f4b69a87dbf765b73ac196e272678da06133daf0"
GOT="$(shasum -a 256 "$PATCH" | awk '{print $1}')"
[ "$GOT" = "$WANT" ] || { echo "!! Patch is corrupt."; echo "   want $WANT"; echo "   got  $GOT"; exit 1; }
echo "== patch verified"
git apply --check -C1 "$PATCH" || { echo "!! Patch does not apply cleanly. Nothing written."; exit 1; }
git apply -C1 "$PATCH"
echo "== applied"

cd together-city-react
npx tsc --noEmit
npx vitest run
node scripts/a11y-audit.mjs
node scripts/motion-ceiling.mjs
node scripts/lint-ceiling.mjs
npx vite build
cd ..

git add together-city-react/src/features/beauty/components/PhotoStudio.tsx \
        together-city-react/src/features/beauty/pages/Profile.tsx \
        together-city-react/src/app/photo-gate.test.ts
git commit -F - <<'MSG'
Three photographs, taken however suits you

To get a word out of the skin & hair assessment you had to supply six
photographs — face, left side, right side, hairline, top of head, scalp
close-up — every one of them mandatory, each one a click on a tile that opened
a file browser. Two of them cannot be taken of yourself at all without a second
person or a mirror. It is a photoshoot standing in front of a product.

IT IS THREE NOW, AND ONLY TWO ARE REQUIRED. A full face with hair, a skin
close-up, and — if there is one — the thing that is actually bothering them.
The third is optional because "a concern" is conditional by definition:
somebody with nothing bothering them has nothing to photograph, and making them
find a third picture in order to pass a gate is precisely the rigidity being
removed. The required pair sits first, so filling the grid left to right ends
exactly where the gate is satisfied.

THE METER COUNTS THE REQUIRED ONES ONLY. It would otherwise read 2/3 to
somebody who is finished, or 3/2 to somebody who is generous. `requiredCount`
and `photosReady` are the same rule read two ways, and the sentence under the
button now NAMES what is missing rather than counting it — "Add 1 more photo"
on a grid with an empty optional tile in it is an instruction you can follow and
still be locked out.

THREE WAYS IN, ONE PATH THROUGH. Choose a file, drop one on a tile, or take one
with the camera. All three end at the same `readShot()` and produce the same
~1280px JPEG; the resize is not decoration, a phone photo is 3–8 MB and the
request cap is 4 MB an image. A second resize written for the camera is how the
two would come to differ.

THE CAMERA IS A CAMERA, NOT `capture=""`. The cheap version of this feature is
an attribute on the file input, which does nothing at all on a desktop and on a
phone hands you to the system camera app and back. This is getUserMedia with a
live preview, a shutter, a flip between front and back, and a review step —
because a shutter that files the photo straight into the grid gives you no way
to notice you blinked. Failure is a sentence, not a dead overlay: no camera, no
permission or an insecure origin all say so and point at Choose.

TWO DETAILS IN THERE THAT ARE EASY TO GET WRONG, AND ARE THE WHOLE DIFFERENCE.
The preview is mirrored and the photograph is not — every front camera anybody
has used behaves this way, and a saved selfie with the parting on the wrong side
is a picture of somebody else; the flip is CSS on the video and nowhere near the
canvas. And the MediaStream's tracks are stopped from the effect's cleanup, so
they stop on close, on unmount and on a flip alike. A camera light still on
after the overlay is gone is the most alarming thing a web page can do.

DROPPING SPILLS. Drop three files on the first tile and it keeps the first and
hands the rest to whichever tiles are still empty, in order, because what people
actually do is select their photos and drag the lot over — and a grid that keeps
one and silently discards two has punished them for it.

THE SERVER DID NOT CHANGE, WHICH IS WORTH SAYING OUT LOUD. `slot` has always
been `z.string().min(1).max(32)` with a cap of eight, stored verbatim beside the
findings; no endpoint names an angle. "Reduce the required photos" sounds like a
contract change and is entirely a frontend one.

THE SHEET WEARS THE STAGE. relief.spec caught the first version with `#fff`,
`#000` and `#111` in it, correctly: `--stage`, `--stage-tile` and the three
`--on-stage` inks already exist for a lit thing on a dark ground, which is what
this is. The remove button is 44px of target around a 28px chip, because the
a11y ceiling wants the tap area and the photograph wants the small mark.

Empty tiles are as tall as what they are asking for; a filled one holds 3:4 so a
face is not cropped square. Three portrait boxes stacked on a phone was most of
a screen of nothing, and it was found by rendering at 390 rather than by
reading.

photo-gate.test.ts guards the one thing that will be broken by somebody tidying:
`Object.keys(pics).length >= 2` looks identical to the gate and passes anybody
who uploaded a face and a concern.

tsc clean, vitest green (55 files, 444 tests), a11y 0 at the ceiling, motion and
lint at theirs, vite build clean. Rendered at 900 and 390.

MSG
echo "== committed"

echo
echo "==============================================================="
echo " Landed: $NEEDS"
echo " Face & hair, a skin close-up, and an optional concern —"
echo " camera, file or drag. Push, and Vercel ships it."
echo "==============================================================="
